<article class="env-lemma" id="03IE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03IE">Lemma <span data-tag="03IE">66.4.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$, $Y$ be algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $X' \subset X$ be an open subspace. Let $f : Y \to X$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then $f$ factors through $X'$ if and only if $|f| : |Y| \to |X|$ factors through $|X'| \subset |X|$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/02YW" data-tag="02YW">65.12.3</a> we see that $Y' = Y \times _ X X' \to Y$ is an open immersion. If $|f|(|Y|) \subset |X'|$, then clearly $|Y'| = |Y|$. Hence $Y' = Y$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/03BZ" data-tag="03BZ">66.4.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>